      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "Rule 8(c)(1), read with Rules 15(a)(2) and 16(b)(4), requires a defendant that omitted an affirmative defense from its answer to obtain leave to add it; lack of prejudice alone does not permit the defendant to bypass the amendment and scheduling-order requirements by first invoking the defense at summary judgment."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The Court states a generally applicable rule for affirmative defenses first raised in dispositive motions after the pleading-amendment deadline, while leaving timely amendments and defenses already fairly pleaded untouched; the holding is not confined to Title VII's personal-staff exemption."
    }
  ],
